17	 * <p>De-duplication: when the computed code already belongs to another owner, {@code -<n>} is
18	 * appended with the smallest {@code n} of 2 or more that makes it unique (so a first
19	 * collision yields {@code <base>-2}, the next {@code <base>-3}, and so on). The owner ends up
20	 * with the de-duplicated {@code customerCode}.
